        "original_id": "83ebd72d-242f-5ceb-84bd-98dc5c602a84",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Ilysiakos B.C.\n- People: Antonis Fotsis\n- Concepts: Greek alphabet, Phoenician alphabet, Elysium\n- Places: Ilissia\n\nFacts:\n- The Greek alphabet was derived from the earlier Phoenician alphabet.\n- The Greek alphabet was the first alphabetic script to have distinct letters for vowels as well as consonants.\n- Antonis Fotsis, also spelled Antonios, was born on April 2, 1981.\n- Antonis Fotsis is a Greek professional basketball player for Ilysiakos.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name is said to reference Elysium.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name and logo begin with the Greek letter Η instead of Ι.\n- Ilissia, where Ilysiakos B.C. is based, begins with the Greek letter Ι.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
